  <h1>The Spray That Almost Killed America's Bird</h1>
  <p class="dek">In 1963, the bald eagle was almost gone from the lower 48 states: 487 nesting pairs left. A single book changed everything. And the bird that almost died for pesticide money now soars over every state in the union.</p>
